  "idea": "Linear Insights update for software engineering velocity tracking",
  "text": "Customer feedback usually dies in support channels, but Linear just automated the entire handoff. Valuable user insights get buried in Slack threads and helpdesks because nobody maintains centralized product logs. That disconnect blinds engineers to recurring software glitches and drives frustrated users to competitors. Linear captures customer signals across Zendesk, Slack, and Front, clustering similar requests into actionable engineering issues. You resolve user friction before it causes churn.",
